-- title:
--   Original stopped controlled Gaussian Taylor expectation has exact half-variance drift
-- statement:
--   On the original source X, filtration and dividend-controlled prepayment reserve leftLim(x + X.X - rightLimit D), under zero Lévy jump measure and bounded stopped predictable gradient/Hessian, the expected discounted ruin-masked Gaussian Taylor cell equals the expected exact (h sigma squared / 2) Hessian drift. This follows from the source-specific accepted stopped-history conditional Gaussian theorem and integral_condExp. No detached Brownian model or positive sigma assumption.
-- source:
--   W7-05: exact corollary of Proved 6242d57f-1e88-4cec-8f52-6ddc12acf9d0 and pinned Mathlib integral_condExp, same original Ω/P/X/filtration/control/ruin mask.

